          <mxGeometry height="40" width="260" x="-2309" y="-73.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-207" parent="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-206" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;" value="Accepted_At" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="130" x="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-208" connectable="0" parent="1" style="group" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="340" x="-2389" y="-25.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-209" parent="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-208" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;" value="Type" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="130" x="210" y="22.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-210" edge="1" parent="1" source="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-212" style="edgeStyle=none;shape=connector;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=default;strokeWidth=1.5;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=page;resizable=0;endArrow=none;endFill=0;" target="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-57">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-2677.0310880829015" y="81.015544041451" as="sourcePoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-211" connectable="0" parent="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-210" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];inheritText=1;fontSize=13;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=page;" value="1..1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.9252" y="4" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="28" y="-4" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-212" parent="1" style="shape=rhombus;perimeter=rhombusPerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;" value="IS_FOR" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="-2609" y="49.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dBaTeAzhe4pxGJI8UXW5-213" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=2;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;strong&gt;BR1.&lt;/strong&gt; Every ACCOUNT has at least one role (RESIDENT, VOLUNTEER or both). A second role is activated on the same account, never a duplicate account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR2.&lt;/strong&gt; Registration and role activation record a TERMS_ACCEPTANCE, so every account has at least one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR3.&lt;/strong&gt; Account_ID is unique across all accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR4.&lt;/strong&gt; Account_ID, First_Name, Last_Name, Public_Name, and Date_Of_Birth are required for all accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR5.&lt;/strong&gt; Address is required for a RESIDENT account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR6.&lt;/strong&gt; The account holder must be 18 or older, and Date_Of_Birth cannot be in the future. Age is derived from Date_Of_Birth.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR7.&lt;/strong&gt; Postal_Code has six characters (for example T2P1J9) and the Address must be in Calgary.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR8.&lt;/strong&gt; A RESIDENT cannot change their profile address while they have a pickup request that is not yet collected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR9.&lt;/strong&gt; A VOLUNTEER saves 0 to 3 distinct Preferred_Postal_Code values. Saved codes trigger matching notifications unless the account is deactivated; with none saved, no new-request match notifications are generated for that Volunteer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR10.&lt;/strong&gt; A NOTIFICATION belongs to exactly one account and is used to deliver in-app and push notifications.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR11.&lt;/b&gt; Each ECOPOINTS_AWARD is earned through exactly one role: by a VOLUNTEER or by a RESIDENT. A delivery creates a volunteer award and a resident award. When a volunteer delivers their own request, their account receives both. A resident’s cancellation outside the cancellation window creates a volunteer award only. The cancellation window is the period more than 24 hours before the start of the assignment’s pic&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;kup window. No cancellation award is created when the volunteer is also the request’s resident.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR12.&lt;/strong&gt; Combined_Ecopoints (ACCOUNT) is derived: the sum of Points over all ECOPOINTS_AWARDs the account has earned in either role, as a RESIDENT and as a VOLUNTEER, including delivery and cancellation awards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR13.&lt;/strong&gt; A RESIDENT owns the requests they create, and the owner never changes. Only the owning resident can confirm a collection while the request is Assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR14.&lt;/strong&gt; Every ASSIGNMENT belongs to exactly one VOLUNTEER, and a volunteer can accept a request created by their own account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR15.&lt;/strong&gt; Public profiles show only Public_Name, Account_ID, roles, ecopoints and member since (Created_At). Legal name, email, birth date, address and PICKUP_REQUEST details (quantity, item category, etc.) stay private.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR16.&lt;/strong&gt; Every PICKUP_REQUEST has at least one STATUS_CHANGE; the first one records Open when the request is created.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR17.&lt;/strong&gt; A STATUS_CHANGE is added each time the request status changes, including expiry and reopening, and is never edited. Reason is optional and explains the change, for example, expired or missed pickup.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR18.&lt;/strong&gt; STATUS_CHANGE is weak: it is identified by its PICKUP_REQUEST plus Changed_At. Status is one of Open, Assigned, Collected, Delivered, Cancelled, Expired, Missed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR19.&lt;/strong&gt; An ASSIGNMENT links one VOLUNTEER, one PICKUP_REQUEST and one PICKUP_WINDOW, which must be one of the windows that request offers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;BR20.&lt;/b&gt; A PICKUP_REQUEST has at most one ASSIGNMENT that hasn’t ended (Ended_At empty) at a time. Ended assignments are kept for history.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR21.&lt;/strong&gt; ASSIGNMENT: Collected_At is set when the owning resident confirms collection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR22. &lt;/b&gt;An ASSIGNMENT can be cancelled or reported missed only before Collected_At is set. A missed pickup can be reported only after the selected window ends. A resident can cancel the request or its assignment only until the selected window ends; after that they confirm collection or report a missed pickup. A volunteer can cancel any time before Collected_At is set. If an assignment is cancelled by the resident or the volunteer, the request returns to Open if valid future windows remain, otherwise it becomes Expired; the resident may offer new windows. If a missed pickup is reported, the request becomes Missed, a final status, and the resident may reschedule, which creates a new PICKUP_REQUEST linked to the missed one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR23.&lt;/strong&gt; ASSIGNMENT: Ended_At and End_Reason are set together. End_Reason is one of Delivered, Volunteer_Cancelled, Resident_Cancelled, Missed_Pickup.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR24.&lt;/strong&gt; ASSIGNMENT: Status is derived: &quot;Active&quot; if Collected_At and Ended_At are empty, &quot;Collected&quot; if only Collected_At is set, otherwise the End_Reason.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR25.&lt;/strong&gt; A DELIVERY is recorded only for a collected ASSIGNMENT, by its volunteer. An ASSIGNMENT has at most one DELIVERY.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR26.&lt;/strong&gt; DELIVERY: Delivered_At cannot be earlier than Collected_At.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR27.&lt;/strong&gt; A DELIVERY is recorded only when the facility accepts the items; items a facility refuses are handled outside the app.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR28.&lt;/strong&gt; A DELIVERY can only go to a facility that accepts the request&#39;s ITEM_CATEGORY.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR29.&lt;/strong&gt; Each assignment requires exactly one acknowledgment of the terms, a TERMS_ACCEPTANCE of Type AT_VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTANCE, made by the assignment&#39;s Volunteer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR30.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Quantity is a positive integer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR31.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Estimated_Weight_Kg = Quantity × Standard_Weight_Kg (2 decimals). It&#39;s computed by the system and recalculated on edit (FR06, FR10). Changing Standard_Weight_Kg does not update existing requests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR32.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: A request offers 1–3 windows that don&#39;t overlap and start in the future, each with one hourly slot (0-23) based on the starting hour of the day, ending no later than Created_At + 30 days (FR07).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR33.&lt;/b&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Expires_At = the start of its last active PICKUP_WINDOW, recalculated when the active windows change (FR10). Every window ends by Created_At + 30 days (BR32), so a request never stays Open past 30 days, and reopening doesn’t move that limit. Only Open requests expire (FR20).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR34.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Pickup_Address is copied from the resident&#39;s profile at creation and never changes (FR07, FR10).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR35.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Only Open requests can be edited (FR10, BR45).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR36.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_WINDOW: Replaced windows are kept with Is_Active = false, for assignment history.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR37.&lt;/strong&gt; ITEM_CATEGORY: each category has one Name (for example, AA battery, cell phone, refrigerator) and exactly one Waste_Type that classifies it (for example, Battery, Electronics, Appliance). Categories are predefined.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR38.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: A Resident must acknowledge the safety requirements before creating a Pickup Request. The acknowledgment is mandatory and recorded with the request through its TERMS_ACCEPTANCE.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR39.&lt;/strong&gt; RECYCLING_FACILITY: Facilities are predefined; residents and volunteers can&#39;t create them (FR17).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR40.&lt;/strong&gt; PUSH_SUBSCRIPTION: A Push Subscription must be deleted when its account logs out on that device, when its account is deactivated, or when the push service returns 404 or 410 upon sending a push.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR41.&lt;/strong&gt; Volunteer Points = (3 × Quantity) + (4 × Estimated_Weight_Kg). Resident Points = Volunteer Points ÷ 2, with no rounding. A cancellation award uses the Volunteer formula. Points are stored with 2 decimals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR42.&lt;/strong&gt; Accounts are deactivated, not deleted. Their history is kept.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR43.&lt;/strong&gt; Creating a PICKUP_REQUEST records a TERMS_ACCEPTANCE of Type AT_RESIDENT_REQUEST_CREATION for the creating Resident.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR44.&lt;/strong&gt; Recording a DELIVERY also sets Ended_At and End_Reason = Delivered. Delivered_At is derived from Ended_At.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR45.&lt;/strong&gt; A request&#39;s current Status comes from its latest STATUS_CHANGE.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR46.&lt;/strong&gt; When a request&#39;s status changes, the related accounts are notified, except accounts that are deactivated (BR47).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR47.&lt;/strong&gt; NOTIFICATION objects are deleted upon deactivation of their linked account.&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;BR48.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt; Each ECOPOINTS_AWARD creates one NOTIFICATION for the account that earns it, unless that account is deactivated (BR47). Each NOTIFICATION comes from exactly one source: a PICKUP_REQUEST or an ECOPOINTS_AWARD.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR49.&lt;/strong&gt; A NOTIFICATION about a request is expired when that request moves past the state it describes. Expired notifications are hidden and deleted daily. EcoPoints notifications never expire. They are deleted only with their account (BR47).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR50.&lt;/strong&gt; A Missed PICKUP_REQUEST can be rescheduled once, while reporting the miss, by creating a new PICKUP_REQUEST that references it. The new request copies the category, quantity, notes and photo; takes the address from the profile; records a new terms acceptance; and has its own Created_At and Expires_At.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR51.&lt;/strong&gt; An item photo is visible to the request owner and to Volunteers while the request is Open, then to the owner and the assigned Volunteer. A delivery photo is visible only to the owner and the delivering Volunteer. Location metadata is removed before upload. A photo file is deleted only when no request references it. A PICKUP_REQUEST photo is optional; a DELIVERY photo is required (FR17).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR52.&lt;/strong&gt; Is_Read is set by the user (one notification or all).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR53. &lt;/b&gt;An account can’t be deactivated while it owns an Open, Assigned or Collected request or is the volunteer of an assignment that hasn’t ended (Ended_At empty).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR54.&lt;/strong&gt; A TERMS_ACCEPTANCE must reference the current TERMS_DOCUMENT at the time of acceptance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR55.&lt;/strong&gt; An ASSIGNMENT has at most one ECOPOINTS_AWARD per role.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR56.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Email is stored only in Firebase, under the account’s Account_ID (the Firebase uid), and Firebase enforces that it’s unique.&amp;nbsp;Role membership (RESIDENT, VOLUNTEER) is also copied to Firebase as custom claims.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR57:&lt;/strong&gt; Awarded_At and Type on ECOPOINTS_AWARD are derived from the assignment.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR58.&lt;/strong&gt; NOTIFICATION: Title and Body are derived, never stored. When the notification is sent (SSE and push), Title and Body are built from the event that created it. When the notification list is read, Title and Body are built from the related request, assignment or award. The assignment is the request’s latest one for resident notifications, the recipient’s latest one on that request for volunteer notifications, and the award’s assignment for EcoPoints notifications; this is unambiguous because older notifications expire (BR49). Metadata holds only facts stored nowhere else: the event’s Request_Seq, its action id, and for request edits the reason and changed fields. Title and Body never include a street address or photo link (NFR03).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BR59.&lt;/strong&gt; PICKUP_REQUEST: Deliverable_Facilities is derived: the RECYCLING_FACILITIES that accept the request’s ITEM_CATEGORY.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR60&lt;/b&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;Each PHOTO is linked either to one or more requests or to exactly one delivery, never both.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR61.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;PICKUP_REQUEST: Request_Seq starts at 1 and increases by 1 for every event published about the request (two events from one action get consecutive numbers). A rescheduled request starts at 1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="2090" width="777.74" x="-3170" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
